468801212905,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":16.6,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.24976356224967833,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":58.4,"_gate_incr_roic":0.08961375701820443,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":46.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.027320365284894746,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":24.2,"_gate_pool_share":0.021671974742379918,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":48.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10572594738111452,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":77.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0031116933327589467,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":46.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0035179388143195306,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.014763335200228545,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":68.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0015389743874659704,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.0086,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.8,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":80.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Asbury Automotive Group, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an automotive retailer in the United States. It operates through Dealerships; and Total Care Auto, Powered by Asbury (TCA) segments. The company offers a range of automotive products and services, including new and used vehicles; and vehicle repair and maintenance services, replacement parts, collision repair, and reconditioning services for used vehicles. It also provides finance and insurance products, including arranging vehicle financing through third parties; and aftermarket products, such as extended vehicle service contracts, guaranteed asset protection debt cancellation, prepaid maintenance contracts, key replacement contracts, paintless dent repair contracts, appearance protection contracts, tire and wheel, and lease wear and tear contracts. The company sells its products and services to individual retail customers, other dealers, and licensed wholesalers through its network of dealerships, as well as at auctions. Asbury Automotive Group, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel E. Clara | CEO, President & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 15K people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Asbury Automotive Group Inc is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.6B market cap on $18.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 48% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.9M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To Asbury Automotive Group (ABG) Weaker Quarterly Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/retail/nyse-abg/asbury-automotive-group/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-asbury-automotive-group-abg-we","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793982427.504,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Asbury Automotive Group, Inc. (NYSE:ABG) Stock Has Average Price Target of $220.88","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/asb