rs: P/E 8.0 vs 19.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 5% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an EBIT/EV of 9.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $224 on average, 10% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 11% earns above the cost of capital of 8.2%, but the 3pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.25).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.58x.","ROE of 13% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (3.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.3x net debt to EBITDA ($104.7M of cash against $3.1B of debt), with interest covered 3.1x.","The current ratio of 0.95 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.3% over 3 years, 20.3% over 5 years and 10.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 30%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 8%.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (1.0% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.9%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 4 purchases and 1 sale over the past year, net $919K bought.","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.4% (0.4% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 12.5% of the float, 4.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 15,000 employees, each generates about $1.2M of revenue, 3.2x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 10.8% a year.","CEO pay is $1.8M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":68,"head":"Invest: trades 48% below fair value of $393; revenue grew 20.3%/yr over 5y.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 45, gates 13/26)","Trades 48% below fair value of $393","Revenue grew 20.3%/yr over 5y","P/E 8.0x vs sector 19.3x","Insiders net buyers ($919K over 12 months)"],"cons":["Net debt/EBITDA 3.3x","12-1 month momentum -25%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":333.8,"vc":{"base":392.71,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":392.71,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.1212,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"ABG","date":"2026-11-06"}